  "id": "IE-E2C-011",
  "title": "广场与升旗（The Square and the Flag-Raising Ceremony）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "B: Oh, how spacious it is! I've heard so much about the Square. Now I have the pleasure of seeing it with my own eyes. A: The total area of the square is 44 hectares and it is the largest city center square in the world today. B: Oh, dear! It is really much larger than I expected. I think it is one of the most pleasing city squares in the world. A: I think so. Along the central north-south axis, firstly we can see the national flagpole. It is made of 4 seamless steel tubes, 32.6 meters high, and 7 tons in weight. Since May 1, 1991, we have the flag-raising ceremony at sunrise and the flag-lowering ceremony at sunset every day. B: I think it must be very impressive. A: Yes, the ceremonies are brief but solemn. Every morning, when the sun is about to rise, the guard of honor of the National Flag march out of Tian'anmen Rostrum to the square and raise the flag exactly at sunrise. Accompanied by the National Anthem, the bright Five-Star Red Flag rises slowly with the sunrise, symbolizing a bright future for China.\n【中文对照】乙：哇，真开阔啊！关于这个广场我听过太多了，今天总算亲眼见到了。甲：广场总面积四十四公顷，是当今世界上最大的城市中心广场。乙：天哪，比我想象的大多了。我觉得这是世界上最令人心旷神怡的城市广场之一。甲：我也这么认为。沿中央南北轴线，首先看到的是国旗杆：旗杆由四根无缝钢管制成，高三十二点六米，重七吨。自 1991 年 5 月 1 日起，每天日出升旗、日落降旗。乙：场面一定非常震撼。甲：是的，升降旗仪式简短而庄严。每天清晨，太阳将出之际，国旗护卫队从天安门城楼走出，列队进入广场，在日出那一刻准时升旗。伴随着国歌，鲜艳的五星红旗与朝阳一同冉冉升起，象征中国光明的未来。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "B: Oh, how spacious it is! I've heard so much about the Square. Now I have the pleasure of seeing it with my own eyes. A: The total area of the square is 44 hectares and it is the largest city center square in the world today. B: Oh, dear! It is really much larger than I expected. I think it is one of the most pleasing city squares in the world. A: I think so. Along the central north-south axis, firstly we can see the national flagpole. It is made of 4 seamless steel tubes, 32.6 meters high, and 7 tons in weight. Since May 1, 1991, we have the flag-raising ceremony at sunrise and the flag-lowering ceremony at sunset every day. B: I think it must be very impressive. A: Yes, the ceremonies are brief but solemn. Every morning, when the sun is about to rise, the guard of honor of the National Flag march out of Tian'anmen Rostrum to the square and raise the flag exactly at sunrise. Accompanied by the National Anthem, the bright Five-Star Red Flag rises slowly with the sunrise, symbolizing a bright future for China.",
  "ref": "乙：哇，真开阔啊！关于这个广场我听过太多了，今天总算亲眼见到了。甲：广场总面积四十四公顷，是当今世界上最大的城市中心广场。乙：天哪，比我想象的大多了。我觉得这是世界上最令人心旷神怡的城市广场之一。甲：我也这么认为。沿中央南北轴线，首先看到的是国旗杆：旗杆由四根无缝钢管制成，高三十二点六米，重七吨。自 1991 年 5 月 1 日起，每天日出升旗、日落降旗。乙：场面一定非常震撼。甲：是的，升降旗仪式简短而庄严。每天清晨，太阳将出之际，国旗护卫队从天安门城楼走出，列队进入广场，在日出那一刻准时升旗。伴随着国歌，鲜艳的五星红旗与朝阳一同冉冉升起，象征中国光明的未来。",
  "anchor": "",
  "context": "所属模块：口译；出处：2026备考材料·05-英译汉篇章",
