  "id": "IE-E2C-015",
  "title": "长廊与排云殿（The Long Corridor and the Hall of Dispelling Clouds）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "B: It must be the famous Long Corridor. I've seen it many times on postcards. A: Yes. As the longest corridor in China, it starts from the Gate of Greeting the Moon in the east and ends at Shizhang Pavilion in the west, covering a distance of 728 meters with 273 sections. (looking at paintings on the crossbeams of the Long Corridor) B: Wow, it is really long. What are these paintings? I don't understand them at all. A: These colorful paintings consist of four kinds: landscapes and scenic spots; beautiful flowers and birds; Chinese architectures; human figures and classical stories. It's not easy to understand all of them. B: Anyway, I think the paintings of the corridor are delicate and scenes are fine. A: Ms. Green, you know the Long Corridor was built on the slope of the hill. Did you notice the rises and falls of the terrain? B: No, I can hardly notice that. How could it be? A: As a matter of fact, the Long Corridor was designed to follow the physical features of the southern slope of Longevity Hill and four octagonal, double-eave pavilions, symbolizing four seasons of a year, were all built on the junctions of rises and falls, twists and turns. Thus you will not feel the rises and falls or the twists and turns when you are walking along the long corridor. B: Oh, I see. The structure of the Long Corridor is really unique. It separates the mountain and lake and it's a shelter against the wind and sun while people enjoy the sights. A: Exactly. Now we are approaching the center of the Long Corridor which intersects at the central axis of Longevity Hill. This area is the most magnificent area in the Summer Palace because of its distinctive layout. There lies in succession the Gate of Dispelling Clouds, the Hall of Dispelling Clouds and the Tower of Buddhist Incense. All of them are built on a central axis and each is taller than its predecessor. This was designed to give prominence to the last one, the Tower of Buddhist Incense.\n【中文对照】乙：这一定就是著名的长廊了，我在明信片上见过好多次。甲：是的。长廊是中国最长的廊，东起邀月门，西至石丈亭，全长七百二十八米，共二百七十三间。（看着长廊横梁上的彩画）乙：哇，真长啊。这些画是什么？我一点儿也看不懂。甲：这些彩画分为四类：山水风景、花鸟鱼虫、中国建筑、人物典故，想全都弄明白可不容易。乙：不过长廊的彩画真精致，景致也美。甲：格林女士，长廊是依万寿山南坡而建的，您注意到地势的起伏了吗？乙：没有，我几乎没感觉到，这是怎么回事？甲：实际上，长廊的设计顺应了万寿山南坡的自然地形，四座八角重檐亭象征一年四季，都建在地势起伏、廊身曲折的连接点上，所以您漫步廊中时感觉不到高低起伏和曲折变化。乙：哦，明白了。长廊的结构真是别具匠心：它隔开了山与湖，又是人们游览时遮风避阳的凉棚。甲：正是如此。现在我们快到长廊中心了，这里正与万寿山的中轴线相交。这一带布局独特，是颐和园最壮观的区域：排云门、排云殿、佛香阁依次排列，都建在同一中轴线上，而且一座比一座高——这是为了突出最后一座建筑：佛香阁。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "B: It must be the famous Long Corridor. I've seen it many times on postcards. A: Yes. As the longest corridor in China, it starts from the Gate of Greeting the Moon in the east and ends at Shizhang Pavilion in the west, covering a distance of 728 meters with 273 sections. (looking at paintings on the crossbeams of the Long Corridor) B: Wow, it is really long. What are these paintings? I don't understand them at all. A: These colorful paintings consist of four kinds: landscapes and scenic spots; beautiful flowers and birds; Chinese architectures; human figures and classical stories. It's not easy to understand all of them. B: Anyway, I think the paintings of the corridor are delicate and scenes are fine. A: Ms. Green, you know the Long Corridor was built on the slope of the hill. Did you notice the rises and falls of the terrain? B: No, I can hardly notice that. How could it be? A: As a matter of fact, the Long Corridor was designed to follow the physical features of the southern slope of Longevity Hill and four octagonal, double-eave pavilions, symbolizing four seasons of a year, were all built on the junctions of rises and falls, twists and turns. Thus you will not feel the rises and falls or the twists and turns when you are walking along the long corridor. B: Oh, I see. The structure of the Long Corridor is really unique. It separates the mountain and lake and it's a shelter against the wind and sun while people enjoy the sights. A: Exactly. Now we are approaching the center of the Long Corridor which intersects at the central axis of Longevity Hill. This area is the most magnificent area in the Summer Palace because of its distinctive layout. There lies in succession the Gate of Dispelling Clouds, the Hall of Dispelling Clouds and the Tower of Buddhist Incense. All of them are built on a central axis and each is taller than its predecessor. This was designed to give prominence to the last one, the Tower of Buddhist Incense.",
  "ref": "乙：这一定就是著名的长廊了，我在明信片上见过好多次。甲：是的。长廊是中国最长的廊，东起邀月门，西至石丈亭，全长七百二十八米，共二百七十三间。（看着长廊横梁上的彩画）乙：哇，真长啊。这些画是什么？我一点儿也看不懂。甲：这些彩画分为四类：山水风景、花鸟鱼虫、中国建筑、人物典故，想全都弄明白可不容易。乙：不过长廊的彩画真精致，景致也美。甲：格林女士，长廊是依万寿山南坡而建的，您注意到地势的起伏了吗？乙：没有，我几乎没感觉到，这是怎么回事？甲：实际上，长廊的设计顺应了万寿山南坡的自然地形，四座八角重檐亭象征一年四季，都建在地势起伏、廊身曲折的连接点上，所以您漫步廊中时感觉不到高低起伏和曲折变化。乙：哦，明白了。长廊的结构真是别具匠心：它隔开了山与湖，又是人们游览时遮风避阳的凉棚。甲：正是如此。现在我们快到长廊中心了，这里正与万寿山的中轴线相交。这一带布局独特，是颐和园最壮观的区域：排云门、排云殿、佛香阁依次排列，都建在同一中轴线上，而且一座比一座高——这是为了突出最后一座建筑：佛香阁。",
