  "id": "IE-E2C-016",
  "title": "祈年殿形制（The Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "A: Okay. The hall is cone-shaped structure with triple eaves and a gilded knob on it, which symbolizes the supreme power of the emperor. It is 32 meters high, 30 meters in diameter. The base of the hall is 6 meters high, triple-tiered circular stone terrace with carved marble balusters on each tier. In traditional Chinese culture, the idea that the Heaven was round, the Earth was square, was well-accepted by ancient people. This is why the temples and altars in the Temple of Heaven are round, while the walls surrounded the temples and altars are square. B: I see. And I also can figure out why the roofs of the main building here are dark blue, while the roofs in the Forbidden City are golden. The dark blue glazed tiles symbolize the clear sky. I'm wondering how the ancient Chinese people made the architectures with such profound cultural connotations. A: Well, believe it or not, the Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests is completely made of wood without use of steel, cement or even the use of a single nail. Supported merely by 28 pillars and adopted the simple technique, a dovetail structure, the hall is considered as one of the architectural miracles in the Temple of Heaven.\n【中文对照】甲：好的。祈年殿是一座三重檐、上冠鎏金宝顶的锥形建筑，象征皇帝至高无上的权力。殿高三十二米，直径三十米；殿基高六米，为三层圆形石台，每层都围有雕花汉白玉栏杆。在中国传统文化中，\"天圆地方\"的观念为古人普遍接受，所以天坛里的殿宇和祭坛都是圆形，而围墙则是方形。乙：明白了。我还能想明白为什么这里主要建筑的屋顶是深蓝色，而故宫的屋顶是金黄色——深蓝琉璃瓦象征晴朗的天空。真想知道古人是怎么造出文化内涵如此深厚的建筑的。甲：这个嘛，信不信由你——祈年殿完全是木结构建筑，不用钢筋、水泥，甚至没用一颗钉子。全殿仅由二十八根柱子支撑，采用榫卯这一简单工艺，堪称天坛的建筑奇迹之一。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "A: Okay. The hall is cone-shaped structure with triple eaves and a gilded knob on it, which symbolizes the supreme power of the emperor. It is 32 meters high, 30 meters in diameter. The base of the hall is 6 meters high, triple-tiered circular stone terrace with carved marble balusters on each tier. In traditional Chinese culture, the idea that the Heaven was round, the Earth was square, was well-accepted by ancient people. This is why the temples and altars in the Temple of Heaven are round, while the walls surrounded the temples and altars are square. B: I see. And I also can figure out why the roofs of the main building here are dark blue, while the roofs in the Forbidden City are golden. The dark blue glazed tiles symbolize the clear sky. I'm wondering how the ancient Chinese people made the architectures with such profound cultural connotations. A: Well, believe it or not, the Hall of Prayer for Good Harvests is completely made of wood without use of steel, cement or even the use of a single nail. Supported merely by 28 pillars and adopted the simple technique, a dovetail structure, the hall is considered as one of the architectural miracles in the Temple of Heaven.",
  "ref": "甲：好的。祈年殿是一座三重檐、上冠鎏金宝顶的锥形建筑，象征皇帝至高无上的权力。殿高三十二米，直径三十米；殿基高六米，为三层圆形石台，每层都围有雕花汉白玉栏杆。在中国传统文化中，\"天圆地方\"的观念为古人普遍接受，所以天坛里的殿宇和祭坛都是圆形，而围墙则是方形。乙：明白了。我还能想明白为什么这里主要建筑的屋顶是深蓝色，而故宫的屋顶是金黄色——深蓝琉璃瓦象征晴朗的天空。真想知道古人是怎么造出文化内涵如此深厚的建筑的。甲：这个嘛，信不信由你——祈年殿完全是木结构建筑，不用钢筋、水泥，甚至没用一颗钉子。全殿仅由二十八根柱子支撑，采用榫卯这一简单工艺，堪称天坛的建筑奇迹之一。",
