  "id": "IE-E2C-020",
  "title": "神路与石牌坊（The Sacred Way and the Marble Archway）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "B: Could you tell me why it's called Sacred Way? A: It means the road leading to Heaven. The emperor, known as the Son of Heaven, went through the sacred road to the sacrificial altar to worship Heaven during his reign. Naturally, after his death, he would also go through the Sacred Way back to heaven. B: I see. What is the structure over there? A: It's the Marble Archway, which is the first structure along the Sacred Way. And it is also a symbol and the starting point of the tomb area. B: When was it built? A: It was built in 1540, during the reign of Jiajing in the Ming Dynasty, served as a monumental construction to eulogize the merits and virtues of the feudal rulers. B: It looks very high, isn't it? A: Yeah, it is 14 meters high and 29 meters wide, and the 5 arches are supported by 6 marble pillars with beautiful relief carvings of dragons and clouds, lions and lotus flowers. In China, it is the best-preserved stone archway.\n【中文对照】乙：您能告诉我这里为什么叫神路吗？甲：意思是通往天界的路。皇帝号称\"天子\"，生前经神路前往祭坛祭天；自然地，他死后也要经由神路返回天界。乙：明白了。那边那座建筑是什么？甲：那是石牌坊，是神路上的第一座建筑，也是陵区的标志和起点。乙：它是什么时候建的？甲：建于 1540 年，即明代嘉靖年间，是一座颂扬封建统治者功德的纪念性建筑。乙：看起来很高啊？甲：是啊，石牌坊高十四米、宽二十九米，五道拱门由六根汉白玉石柱支撑，柱上雕有云龙、石狮和莲花的精美浮雕。这可是中国保存最完好的石牌坊。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "B: Could you tell me why it's called Sacred Way? A: It means the road leading to Heaven. The emperor, known as the Son of Heaven, went through the sacred road to the sacrificial altar to worship Heaven during his reign. Naturally, after his death, he would also go through the Sacred Way back to heaven. B: I see. What is the structure over there? A: It's the Marble Archway, which is the first structure along the Sacred Way. And it is also a symbol and the starting point of the tomb area. B: When was it built? A: It was built in 1540, during the reign of Jiajing in the Ming Dynasty, served as a monumental construction to eulogize the merits and virtues of the feudal rulers. B: It looks very high, isn't it? A: Yeah, it is 14 meters high and 29 meters wide, and the 5 arches are supported by 6 marble pillars with beautiful relief carvings of dragons and clouds, lions and lotus flowers. In China, it is the best-preserved stone archway.",
  "ref": "乙：您能告诉我这里为什么叫神路吗？甲：意思是通往天界的路。皇帝号称\"天子\"，生前经神路前往祭坛祭天；自然地，他死后也要经由神路返回天界。乙：明白了。那边那座建筑是什么？甲：那是石牌坊，是神路上的第一座建筑，也是陵区的标志和起点。乙：它是什么时候建的？甲：建于 1540 年，即明代嘉靖年间，是一座颂扬封建统治者功德的纪念性建筑。乙：看起来很高啊？甲：是啊，石牌坊高十四米、宽二十九米，五道拱门由六根汉白玉石柱支撑，柱上雕有云龙、石狮和莲花的精美浮雕。这可是中国保存最完好的石牌坊。",
  "anchor": "",
  "context": "所属模块：口译；出处：2026备考材料·05-英译汉篇章",
  "source": "2026备考材料·口译训练",
  "status": "✅",
  "exam_tip": "1540／14 米／29 米／5 门 6 柱是石牌坊标准数字链（canon：5 间 6 柱 11 楼）；\"生前祭天、身后归天\"的对称逻辑须在译文中保留。",
