  "id": "IE-E2C-023",
  "title": "鸟巢：人文、绿色、科技奥运（The Bird's Nest: Three Olympic Concepts）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "A: Sure. In the National Stadium, the designs of everything are humanistic. The bowl-like stands zone surrounds the field, which is designed to optimize spectator sight lines and minimize distance between seats and the field where action takes place. And rows of the stands distribute scientifically. B: Wang, can the whole game be seen without any visual obstruction no matter where the spectator is seated? A: Yes. What's more, there are more than 200 wheelchair seats intended for the disabled. B: What a considerate design! It gives first consideration to the need of people. A: Yes. In addition, it has been incorporated many methods for conserving water and energy. Just take one aspect for example. Rainwater can be collected for further use by the Bird's Nest. After the rainwater is drained from the rooftop and collected in designated areas, it will go through a treatment process which will render it suitable for recycled use. For example, the rainwater may be used for irrigation purposes, or for restroom water, further satisfying the \"Green Olympics\" concept. B: Oh, I see. What about a \"High-tech Olympics\"? A: Well, the main body of the National Stadium has a design life of 100 years. Its fire resistance capability is first-rate, and it can withstand an eight-magnitude earthquake. The water-resistance capability of its underground project is also first-rate.\n【中文对照】甲：当然可以。国家体育场里，一切设计都以人为本：碗状的看台区环抱赛场，目的是优化观众视线、尽量缩短座位与比赛场地之间的距离，看台的排布也经过科学设计。乙：小王，无论观众坐在哪儿，看比赛都没有视线遮挡吗？甲：是的。不仅如此，场内还设有两百多个轮椅坐席，供残障人士使用。乙：设计真周到，把人的需求放在了第一位。甲：是的。此外，体育场还采用了多种节水节能措施。仅举一例：雨水可以被鸟巢收集再利用——雨水从屋顶排出、汇集到指定区域后，会经过处理达到可循环使用的标准，比如用于灌溉或卫生间用水，进一步体现\"绿色奥运\"的理念。乙：明白了。那\"科技奥运\"呢？甲：国家体育场主体结构的设计使用年限为一百年，防火性能一流，可抗八级地震，地下工程的抗渗性能同样是一流的。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "A: Sure. In the National Stadium, the designs of everything are humanistic. The bowl-like stands zone surrounds the field, which is designed to optimize spectator sight lines and minimize distance between seats and the field where action takes place. And rows of the stands distribute scientifically. B: Wang, can the whole game be seen without any visual obstruction no matter where the spectator is seated? A: Yes. What's more, there are more than 200 wheelchair seats intended for the disabled. B: What a considerate design! It gives first consideration to the need of people. A: Yes. In addition, it has been incorporated many methods for conserving water and energy. Just take one aspect for example. Rainwater can be collected for further use by the Bird's Nest. After the rainwater is drained from the rooftop and collected in designated areas, it will go through a treatment process which will render it suitable for recycled use. For example, the rainwater may be used for irrigation purposes, or for restroom water, further satisfying the \"Green Olympics\" concept. B: Oh, I see. What about a \"High-tech Olympics\"? A: Well, the main body of the National Stadium has a design life of 100 years. Its fire resistance capability is first-rate, and it can withstand an eight-magnitude earthquake. The water-resistance capability of its underground project is also first-rate.",
  "ref": "甲：当然可以。国家体育场里，一切设计都以人为本：碗状的看台区环抱赛场，目的是优化观众视线、尽量缩短座位与比赛场地之间的距离，看台的排布也经过科学设计。乙：小王，无论观众坐在哪儿，看比赛都没有视线遮挡吗？甲：是的。不仅如此，场内还设有两百多个轮椅坐席，供残障人士使用。乙：设计真周到，把人的需求放在了第一位。甲：是的。此外，体育场还采用了多种节水节能措施。仅举一例：雨水可以被鸟巢收集再利用——雨水从屋顶排出、汇集到指定区域后，会经过处理达到可循环使用的标准，比如用于灌溉或卫生间用水，进一步体现\"绿色奥运\"的理念。乙：明白了。那\"科技奥运\"呢？甲：国家体育场主体结构的设计使用年限为一百年，防火性能一流，可抗八级地震，地下工程的抗渗性能同样是一流的。",
