  "id": "IE-E2C-024",
  "title": "周口店北京人遗址（The Peking Man Site at Zhoukoudian）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "A: Okay. There are many archaeological wonders in China, but few can rival Peking Man Site, which was first explored in 1921 by Swedish geologist Johan Gunnar Anderson. Systematic excavations in later years produced significant finds, including three hominid fossil teeth. In 1929, at the same site, Chinese anthropologist Pei Wenzhong struck upon the first complete skullcap of the same early hominid, revealing new clues to the origins of man that thrilled the scientific world. The fossils of molars and skullcap discovered were identified as a new species and genus which were named Sinanthropus pekinensis, also called Homo erectus pekinensis, literally meaning \"Chinese man from Peking\". The cave, where the skull fossils of Peking Man were unearthed in 1929, has been named \"Zhoukoudian Locality 1\", popularly known as \"Peking Man Cave\".\n【中文对照】甲：好的。中国有不少考古奇观，但很少有能与周口店北京人遗址比肩的。遗址由瑞典地质学家安特生于 1921 年最先发掘，此后数年间的系统发掘收获重大，包括三枚古人类牙齿化石。1929 年，还是在这处遗址，中国人类学家裴文中发现了第一枚完整的北京人头盖骨，为人类起源研究提供了新的线索，震动了整个科学界。出土的臼齿和头盖骨化石被鉴定为一个新属新种，命名为\"中国猿人北京种\"（Sinanthropus pekinensis），又称\"北京直立人\"（Homo erectus pekinensis），字面意思是\"来自北京的中国人\"。1929 年出土北京人头盖骨化石的那个洞穴被命名为\"周口店第一地点\"，俗称\"猿人洞\"。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "A: Okay. There are many archaeological wonders in China, but few can rival Peking Man Site, which was first explored in 1921 by Swedish geologist Johan Gunnar Anderson. Systematic excavations in later years produced significant finds, including three hominid fossil teeth. In 1929, at the same site, Chinese anthropologist Pei Wenzhong struck upon the first complete skullcap of the same early hominid, revealing new clues to the origins of man that thrilled the scientific world. The fossils of molars and skullcap discovered were identified as a new species and genus which were named Sinanthropus pekinensis, also called Homo erectus pekinensis, literally meaning \"Chinese man from Peking\". The cave, where the skull fossils of Peking Man were unearthed in 1929, has been named \"Zhoukoudian Locality 1\", popularly known as \"Peking Man Cave\".",
  "ref": "甲：好的。中国有不少考古奇观，但很少有能与周口店北京人遗址比肩的。遗址由瑞典地质学家安特生于 1921 年最先发掘，此后数年间的系统发掘收获重大，包括三枚古人类牙齿化石。1929 年，还是在这处遗址，中国人类学家裴文中发现了第一枚完整的北京人头盖骨，为人类起源研究提供了新的线索，震动了整个科学界。出土的臼齿和头盖骨化石被鉴定为一个新属新种，命名为\"中国猿人北京种\"（Sinanthropus pekinensis），又称\"北京直立人\"（Homo erectus pekinensis），字面意思是\"来自北京的中国人\"。1929 年出土北京人头盖骨化石的那个洞穴被命名为\"周口店第一地点\"，俗称\"猿人洞\"。",
  "anchor": "",
  "context": "所属模块：口译；出处：2026备考材料·05-英译汉篇章",
  "source": "2026备考材料·口译训练",
  "status": "✅",
