  "id": "IE-E2C-025",
  "title": "雍和宫（The Lama Temple）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "A: The Lama Temple is also known as the \"Palace of Harmony and Peace\". It is considered the best Tibetan temple outside of Tibet. Originally, it was constructed in 1694 as the private residence of Emperor Yongzheng before he was crowned in the Qing Dynasty. In 1725, the third year of the third Qing Emperor Yongzheng's reign, it was made an imperial palace for short stays, named Yonghegong. Gong means palace in Chinese. After the death of Emperor Yongzheng, Yonghegong was converted into a lamasery in 1744 and served as a residence for large amounts of monks from Tibet and Mongolia. B: How big is it? A: It occupies an area of 66,400 square meters which equals 16 acres. The temple is described as a mini-palace with its yellow glazed tiles on the roof and red walls surrounding the architectural complex. As a result of the ancient architecture, every element of the temple is entirely symmetrical, with main halls on a north-south axis and wing halls on both sides. It comprises of a courtyard in the south and five main halls in separate courtyards in the north, including the Hall of the Heavenly Kings, the Hall of Harmony and Peace, the Hall of Eternal Blessings, the Hall of the Dharma Wheel and the Pavilion of Ten Thousand Happiness. Furthermore, this splendid temple combines various architectural styles of the Han, Manchu, Mongolian and Tibetan.\n【中文对照】甲：雍和宫又称\"雍和宫\"，被认为是西藏以外最好的藏传佛教寺院。它最初建于 1694 年，是清代雍正皇帝即位前的私邸。1725 年，即清雍正三年，这里被改为皇帝短期驻跸的行宫，赐名\"雍和宫\"——\"宫\"在汉语中就是宫殿的意思。雍正皇帝驾崩后，雍和宫于 1744 年改为喇嘛庙，成为来自西藏和蒙古的大批喇嘛的居所。乙：它有多大？甲：占地六万六千四百平方米，合十六英亩。整座寺庙黄瓦红墙，被称为\"小皇宫\"。作为古建筑群，雍和宫每个部分都完全对称：主殿位于南北轴线上，两侧配殿对称分布。寺庙由南部的一个院落和北部五个分列院落中的主殿组成，包括天王殿、雍和宫殿、永佑殿、法轮殿和万福阁。此外，这座宏伟的寺庙融合了汉、满、蒙古、藏等多种建筑风格。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "A: The Lama Temple is also known as the \"Palace of Harmony and Peace\". It is considered the best Tibetan temple outside of Tibet. Originally, it was constructed in 1694 as the private residence of Emperor Yongzheng before he was crowned in the Qing Dynasty. In 1725, the third year of the third Qing Emperor Yongzheng's reign, it was made an imperial palace for short stays, named Yonghegong. Gong means palace in Chinese. After the death of Emperor Yongzheng, Yonghegong was converted into a lamasery in 1744 and served as a residence for large amounts of monks from Tibet and Mongolia. B: How big is it? A: It occupies an area of 66,400 square meters which equals 16 acres. The temple is described as a mini-palace with its yellow glazed tiles on the roof and red walls surrounding the architectural complex. As a result of the ancient architecture, every element of the temple is entirely symmetrical, with main halls on a north-south axis and wing halls on both sides. It comprises of a courtyard in the south and five main halls in separate courtyards in the north, including the Hall of the Heavenly Kings, the Hall of Harmony and Peace, the Hall of Eternal Blessings, the Hall of the Dharma Wheel and the Pavilion of Ten Thousand Happiness. Furthermore, this splendid temple combines various architectural styles of the Han, Manchu, Mongolian and Tibetan.",
  "ref": "甲：雍和宫又称\"雍和宫\"，被认为是西藏以外最好的藏传佛教寺院。它最初建于 1694 年，是清代雍正皇帝即位前的私邸。1725 年，即清雍正三年，这里被改为皇帝短期驻跸的行宫，赐名\"雍和宫\"——\"宫\"在汉语中就是宫殿的意思。雍正皇帝驾崩后，雍和宫于 1744 年改为喇嘛庙，成为来自西藏和蒙古的大批喇嘛的居所。乙：它有多大？甲：占地六万六千四百平方米，合十六英亩。整座寺庙黄瓦红墙，被称为\"小皇宫\"。作为古建筑群，雍和宫每个部分都完全对称：主殿位于南北轴线上，两侧配殿对称分布。寺庙由南部的一个院落和北部五个分列院落中的主殿组成，包括天王殿、雍和宫殿、永佑殿、法轮殿和万福阁。此外，这座宏伟的寺庙融合了汉、满、蒙古、藏等多种建筑风格。",
  "anchor": "",
  "context": "所属模块：口译；出处：2026备考材料·05-英译汉篇章",
  "source": "2026备考材料·口译训练",
  "status": "✅",
  "exam_tip": "1694 潜邸→1725 行宫→1744 改寺的\"三段年代链\"是雍和宫核心考点；五大殿顺序须按南北轴线依次报出。",
