  "id": "IE-E2C-026",
  "title": "天坛概况（General Information of the Temple of Heaven）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "口译训练卡（中译外/外译中）",
  "text": "Good morning ladies and gentlemen. This morning we are going to visit the Temple of Heaven. It is situated on the east side of Yongdingmennei street, Dongcheng District. The temple was where emperors of the Ming and Qing dynasties worshipped heaven on winter solstice and prayed for good harvests in early spring. Altogether, 654 grand ceremonies were held inside the temple by 22 Ming and Qing emperors. In 1961 the State Council announced the Temple of Heaven as the first batch of cultural relics under the special protection by the Chinese Government. In 1998, the Temple of Heaven was placed on the World Cultural Heritage list by UNESCO. In 2007, the National Tourism Administration rated the Temple of Heaven as \"5A-level national tourist scenic spot.\" Today, the Temple of Heaven is not only the largest and the most complete form of ancient altar building complex for worshipping which still existing in the world, but also a cultural treasure containing ancient Chinese astronomy, calendar, philosophy, architecture and other multidisciplinary. Moreover, it is an important part of the ancient capital style of Beijing, the magnificent Hall of Prayer for Good Harvest has become an important symbol of the ancient capital of Beijing.\n【中文对照】各位早上好！今天上午我们要去参观天坛。天坛位于东城区永定门内大街东侧，是明清两代皇帝冬至祭天、孟春祈谷的场所，明清两代共有二十二位皇帝在此举行大祭六百五十四次。1961 年，国务院将天坛列为第一批全国重点文物保护单位；1998 年，天坛被联合国教科文组织列入《世界遗产名录》；2007 年，国家旅游局将其评为国家 5A 级旅游景区。如今，天坛不仅是世界上现存规模最大、形制最完备的古代祭天建筑群，也是一部融汇中国古代天文、历法、哲学、建筑等多学科的文化宝库。同时，它还是古都风貌的重要组成部分，雄伟的祈年殿已成为北京这座古都的重要标志。",
  "direction": "e2c",
  "src": "Good morning ladies and gentlemen. This morning we are going to visit the Temple of Heaven. It is situated on the east side of Yongdingmennei street, Dongcheng District. The temple was where emperors of the Ming and Qing dynasties worshipped heaven on winter solstice and prayed for good harvests in early spring. Altogether, 654 grand ceremonies were held inside the temple by 22 Ming and Qing emperors. In 1961 the State Council announced the Temple of Heaven as the first batch of cultural relics under the special protection by the Chinese Government. In 1998, the Temple of Heaven was placed on the World Cultural Heritage list by UNESCO. In 2007, the National Tourism Administration rated the Temple of Heaven as \"5A-level national tourist scenic spot.\" Today, the Temple of Heaven is not only the largest and the most complete form of ancient altar building complex for worshipping which still existing in the world, but also a cultural treasure containing ancient Chinese astronomy, calendar, philosophy, architecture and other multidisciplinary. Moreover, it is an important part of the ancient capital style of Beijing, the magnificent Hall of Prayer for Good Harvest has become an important symbol of the ancient capital of Beijing.",
  "ref": "各位早上好！今天上午我们要去参观天坛。天坛位于东城区永定门内大街东侧，是明清两代皇帝冬至祭天、孟春祈谷的场所，明清两代共有二十二位皇帝在此举行大祭六百五十四次。1961 年，国务院将天坛列为第一批全国重点文物保护单位；1998 年，天坛被联合国教科文组织列入《世界遗产名录》；2007 年，国家旅游局将其评为国家 5A 级旅游景区。如今，天坛不仅是世界上现存规模最大、形制最完备的古代祭天建筑群，也是一部融汇中国古代天文、历法、哲学、建筑等多学科的文化宝库。同时，它还是古都风貌的重要组成部分，雄伟的祈年殿已成为北京这座古都的重要标志。",
  "anchor": "",
  "context": "所属模块：口译；出处：2026备考材料·05-英译汉篇章",
  "source": "2026备考材料·口译训练",
  "status": "✅",
  "exam_tip": "\"22 帝 654 次祭祀大礼\"是 canon 裁决口径（不窄化为祭天），译文照此直译；1961/1998/2007 三个年份与\"第一批全国重点文保\"定语须完整。",
