  "ref": "Short passage: Calling the police over a dispute. When a tourist falls into a dispute with a vendor, the guide first separates the two sides and leads the tourist away to avoid a crowd. After learning what happened, he tries to settle it through negotiation; if that fails, he reminds the tourist to complain to the market supervision authority or dial 110, keeping the receipt as proof.",
