  "qa_answer": "Beijing stands at the northern tip of the North China Plain, at about 39 degrees north latitude and 116 degrees east longitude. It is on about the same latitude as Philadelphia in the United States. The city is surrounded by Hebei Province on all sides except the southeast, where it borders Tianjin. It lies about 150 kilometers inland from the Bohai Sea and serves as a major transportation hub of China.\n【中文对照】北京位于华北平原北端，大约北纬 39 度、东经 116 度。它与美国的费城纬度相近。除东南与天津接壤外，其余方向均被河北省环绕。北京距渤海约 150 公里，是中国重要的交通枢纽。",
