  "module": "知识问答（英语）",
  "text": "How large is Beijing, and what does its land consist of?\n【中文对照】北京有多大？土地构成如何？",
  "qa_answer": "Beijing covers an area of about 16,410 square kilometers, of which about 62 percent is mountainous and 38 percent is plain. The built-up city spreads over the plain in the southeast, while the mountains in the west and north carry forests, orchards and scenic areas. The municipality is divided into 16 districts. This land structure explains the saying that Beijing is a city half in the mountains and half on the plain.\n【中文对照】北京总面积约 16410 平方公里，其中约 62% 是山区，38% 是平原。建成区铺展在东南部平原上，西部北部的山区则以森林、果园和景区为主。全市划分为 16 个区。这样的土地结构正应了那句\"半城山色半城平\"。",
