  "text": "What is the terrain feature of Beijing?\n【中文对照】北京的地势特征是什么？",
  "qa_answer": "The terrain of Beijing is high in the northwest and low in the southeast. The Western Hills, an extension of the Taihang Mountains, stand on the west, and the Yanshan Mountains close the north and northeast. The plain in the southeast slopes gently toward the Bohai Sea, like a bay embraced on three sides by mountains. The old saying calls this land a place of commanding importance.\n【中文对照】北京地势西北高、东南低。西部是太行山脉的余脉西山，北部和东北部由燕山山脉环抱。东南部平原缓缓向渤海倾斜，形如三面环山的港湾。古人称这里为形胜之地。",
