  "module": "知识问答（英语）",
  "text": "What is the Bird's Nest?\n【中文对照】国家体育场（鸟巢）是一座怎样的建筑？",
  "qa_answer": "The National Stadium, nicknamed the Bird's Nest for its woven steel lattice, hosted the openings, closings and athletics of both Olympics. Its structure uses about forty-two thousand tons of steel, and at night the red glow inside the lattice makes the city's most famous silhouette.\n【中文对照】国家体育场因编织状钢结构得昵称\"鸟巢\"，两届奥运的开闭幕式与田径赛事均在此举行。用钢约 4.2 万吨，夜间红色灯光透过网格，成为北京最著名的剪影。",
