  "id": "QA-FS-023",
  "title": "问答·景泰蓝（Cloisonné）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "知识问答（英语）",
  "text": "What is cloisonné, and where does its name come from?\n【中文对照】景泰蓝是什么？它的名字从何而来？",
  "qa_answer": "Cloisonné is a Beijing craft that inlays copper wire patterns on a bronze body and fills them with colored enamel. Its Chinese name, Jingtai Lan, comes from the Jingtai reign of the Ming Dynasty in the 1450s, when the blue enamel craft reached its peak. Making one piece needs more than one hundred steps and many days of work. It is a national-level intangible cultural heritage and a classic state gift of China.\n【中文对照】景泰蓝是在铜胎上掐丝、填彩釉的北京工艺。其中文名来自明代景泰年间，当时蓝釉工艺臻于极盛，故称景泰蓝。制作一件要经过一百多道工序、费时多日。它是国家级非物质文化遗产，也是经典的国礼。",
  "anchor": "景泰蓝、铜胎掐丝珐琅、景泰年间、国礼",
