  "id": "QA-FS-035",
  "title": "问答·恭王府博物馆（Prince Gong's Mansion）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "知识问答（英语）",
  "text": "Why is Prince Gong's Mansion called half of the Qing history?\n【中文对照】恭王府为什么被称为\"半部清代史\"？",
  "qa_answer": "Prince Gong's Mansion is called half of the Qing history because its owners recorded the rise and fall of the dynasty. It was first built for Heshen, the richest and most corrupt official of the Qianlong reign, and later became the residence of Prince Gong, Yixin, a key figure of late Qing politics. The mansion keeps the best-preserved prince's layout with gardens, halls and a western-style gate. Historians regard it as a museum of Qing aristocratic life.\n【中文对照】恭王府被称为\"半部清代史\"，因为它的主人们写下了王朝的兴衰。它最初为乾隆朝巨贪和珅而建，后来成为晚清政治关键人物恭亲王奕䜣的府邸。府邸保存最完整的王府格局，有花园、殿堂和西洋门。史家把它看作清代贵族生活的博物馆。",
  "anchor": "恭王府、和珅、恭亲王、半部清代史",
