  "id": "QA-FS-038",
  "title": "问答·大钟寺古钟博物馆（Big Bell Temple Museum）",
  "subject": "科目五 导游服务能力（现场考试）",
  "module": "知识问答（英语）",
  "text": "What can visitors see in the Big Bell Temple Museum?\n【中文对照】大钟寺古钟博物馆里能看到什么？",
  "qa_answer": "The Big Bell Temple Museum, set in Juesheng Temple built in 1733, is the only museum of ancient bells in China. Its treasure is the Yongle Bell, cast in the early Ming, which weighs 46.5 tons and is inscribed with over 227,000 Buddhist characters. The bell rings with a deep sound that travels for kilometers. Exhibits trace the history of Chinese bells from bronze chimes to temple bells.\n【中文对照】大钟寺古钟博物馆设在 1733 年建的觉生寺，是中国唯一的古钟博物馆。镇馆之宝是明初铸造的永乐大钟，重 46.5 吨，钟身铸有 22 万余字佛经。钟声深沉，可传数公里。展览梳理了从青铜编钟到寺庙梵钟的中国钟史。",
  "anchor": "大钟寺、觉生寺、永乐大钟、46.5吨",
